      "brief": "The town's guardian shrine stands on a terrace three and a half metres over the street, reached by a stone stair between moss walls, under a weathered wooden torii hung with pink charm tags. An old camphor tree leans over the hall; the shide are fresh, the ground is swept daily, and there are far more warding charms here than one small town should need. From the terrace edge the whole town reads at once — and the sightline down to the festival field is deliberate, kept, and old.",
